Contract, redaction and guardrail checks
----------------------------------------

[PASS] Shared sanitizer handles text and nested mappings/lists without
mutating the input. A second pass produces the same value and zero new
redactions.

[PASS] Stable marker and counter coverage:
  [REDACTED_EMAIL], [REDACTED_PHONE], [REDACTED_TOKEN],
  [REDACTED_API_KEY], [REDACTED_PASSWORD], [REDACTED_PII].

[PASS] Provider captures and final analysis records contain markers rather
than the email, phone, Bearer token, API key, password or known PII fixtures.
CLI success/error paths, receipts and contract writers apply the same
sanitizer.

[PASS] Two hostile HTTP response cases are detected by observable behavior:
  1. instruction override plus secret exfiltration;
  2. /api/admin plus an out-of-scope system command.
Both are replaced by [QUARANTINED_UNTRUSTED_HTTP_RESPONSE], produce no
follow-up request, and persist only safe reasons/hash/counters. A benign
control is not flagged and is still sanitized.

[PASS] Strict JSON Schema contracts validate RiskDecision,
ApprovalDecision, GuardedResponse and RunEvent. Historical Week 4
ExecutionReceipt v1 records remain valid against the unchanged receipt
schema.

[PASS] State and approval controls:
  - GET without a body reaches ready_to_execute without approval.
  - Every POST or materialized curated payload requires approval.
  - Missing, Reject, invalid input, EOF and timeout fail closed.
  - Reject POST makes 0 transport calls.
  - Approve POST makes exactly 1 call to the trusted Gateway origin.
  - Expired, replayed, used, run/proposal/policy/origin/fingerprint mismatch,
    reused run ID, payload TOCTOU and policy TOCTOU are blocked before network.
  - Approval cannot open admin or an unlisted capability.
  - Runtime origin accepts host=http://localhost:8080 or
    compose=http://envoy:8080 only; direct backend/arbitrary origins fail.

[PASS] Guard configuration that is not callable fails at client preflight.
A runtime response-guard failure after the first response produces no raw
excerpt or GuardedResponse artifact, creates a safe failed event, does not
make a follow-up call, and raises the typed ResponseGuardError.

